00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.480
and we've got some real
stars up on that show

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.350
and that's just Ross Matthews.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.183
- [Drew] Oh.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.544
So,

00:01:35.544 --> 00:01:40.544
one of the things that I
really loved about your journey

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.010
is that it took you a very long time

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:50.010
to reach the level of
success that you reached,

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:54.300
and I think it's something
that I'd be interested to hear

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.630
what you have to say about that to people,

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:02.520
because when it takes a
long time to break through,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.590
what do you say to them to stick with it?

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.300
- Yeah, well, that's the biggest challenge

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.180
is staying interested in the work.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.013
You know,

00:02:10.013 --> 00:02:14.510
you started very early and
both of us are lucky enough

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:19.090
to have found success and
then stepped away for a minute

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:22.574
and then had another chance
to bite the apple again,

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:25.490
and that second bite is the juiciest,

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.220
it's the most delicious,
it's the most long lasting,

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.750
and you know, not many
people have that opportunity.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.770
This is such, it's a tough business,

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:35.270
it's a tough business.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.843
You have to earn it, you know,

00:02:38.912 --> 00:02:41.190
you know, listen, it must
be even harder for you.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.670
You come from a family, a legacy of

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.260
very famous actors in this town,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:52.090
and I can only imagine how
tough for this kid to come up

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.150
and say, I want to do that too,

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.220
and then become the success you are today.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.177
- Well, I think, you know, thank you.

00:03:00.195 --> 00:03:04.500
I think probably adjacent
to the way you felt.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.750
There were a lot of
misconceptions that I was born

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.950
with a silver spoon in my mouth,

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.980
or that I had doors open to me.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.210
My family,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:17.490
in 1975 and 76, when I started working,

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.400
the Barrymores at that point

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.490
were not sort of

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.640
in so much Vogue of
being the Royal family.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.580
It had been a long time,

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.720
unfortunately, most of them had passed.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.630
This was not like, oh, you're a Barrymore,

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.780
well come right this way.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.674
People were like, oh yeah,

00:03:36.674 --> 00:03:38.835
(RuPaul laughs)
The Barrymore.

00:03:38.835 --> 00:03:42.210
And when I was born into this name,

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.450
it was a little washed up,
it was a little old school,

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:50.450
it was 1970s in California,
the glory days were long gone,

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.540
and I felt like I really had
to kind of break past that,

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.890
and I wonder in your childhood, you know,

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.390
what did you feel like when you were born?

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.910
Was there a predestine,
was there a support,

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:11.550
was there something you had
to fight against or prove?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.087
What was it like when you were a kid?

00:04:13.087 --> 00:04:14.939
- You know, I always knew that

00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:16.900
there was something for me.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:21.000
My mother when she was
pregnant with me saw a psychic

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.810
and the psychic said,
you're gonna have a boy

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.150
and he's going to be famous,

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.820
so I grew up with that story.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.970
So I thought, oh, okay, well,
how am I going to do that?

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.020
I didn't know I would become

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.689
the most beautiful drag
queen in the world.

00:04:34.689 --> 00:04:37.927
(audience cheers)

00:04:37.927 --> 00:04:40.330
I'm kidding, I'm kidding, you know.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.650
It's funny, it's funny, but, you know,

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.790
I knew that it was my destiny.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.170
I didn't know how, but I was open to it,

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.850
and what we all have to do is be open

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.370
and be willing to hear the
universe's stage direction.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.853
Your job is to find it.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:05:00.520
Clear space for it, you
have to clear a space.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.410
- [Drew] Now you struggled through school,

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.870
